    "source_semantic_class": "other_normative_clinical_instruction",
    "title_or_context": "/sup> However, invasive hemodynamic evaluation or monitoring can be useful to guide management in carefully selected patients with acute HF who have persistent symptoms despite treatment. This includes patients whose fluid status, perfusion, or systemic or pulmonary vascular resistance is uncertain whose systolic blood pressure (SBP) remains low, or is associated with symptoms, despite initial treatment; whose renal function is worsening with therapy; or who require parenteral vasoactive agents."
  },
